Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 43 CLINICAL DATA  Palpable left breast nodule                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   LEFT BREAST NODULE   BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  95    GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM  PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED SURFACES  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  5    CRIBIFORM TYPE WITH HIGH GRADE NUCLEI AND NECROSIS  PRESENT ADJACENT TO INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  FOCALLY PRESENT AT INKED SURFACES  3  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  4  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  5  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  NOTE  Definite blood vascular or lymphatic invasion is not present  BREAST  LEFT   LEFT BREAST MASS    BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  98    GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION AS MEASURED ON A GLASS SLIDE  PRESENT AT NUMEROUS INKED SUPERIOR AND LATERAL SURFACES  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2    CRIBIFORM TYPE WITH HIGH GRADE NUCLEI AND NECROSIS  PRESENT ADJACENT TO INVASIVE CARCINOMA  PRESENT AT INKED SUPERIOR SURFACE  3  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  4  ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  5  PAPILLARY APOCRINE HYPERPLASIA  NOTE  Definite blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not present  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 07                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   MASS    The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 08 43 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  Left breast nodule  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fragment of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal foci of calcification and a small 0 3cm cyst  A small lesion is present with a vague stellate appearance  measuring 0 5cm in greatest size  Frozen section of this lesion is requested by Dr  Gadd  Tissue submitted entirely in A through J with frozen section in J  Received fresh in a second container and designated  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm fragment of breast tissue  The tissue is inked black  with a superior surface  short stitch  yellow over black and the lateral surface  long stitch  green over black  The medial surface is inked red over black  Sectioned to reveal a white granular poorly defined area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DA