t  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 08 59 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional superior margin  is a piece of fibrous fatty tissue measuring 4 x 1 x 1cm  Inked  cross sectioned and entirely submitted in cassette A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional axillary tissue  is a piece of fatty tissue measuring 5 x 1 x 1cm  containing five lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The smaller lymph nodes are entirely submitted and the larger lymph nodes are bisected and half of each are submitted in B  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a left modified radical mastectomy specimen  weighing 1 230 grams  The breast measures 24 x 21 x 4 5cm  and has a 20 x 8cm ellipse of skin including the nipple  There is a stitch indicating the axillary tail  and another stitch indicating the superior margin  The specimen was inked black and the anterior margin inked blue  Sectioning reveals a firm  stellate  white lesion with punctate yellow areas  that measures REMOVED_DATE x 3 x 1 5cm and extends 0 7cm from the closest margin  deep margin   2cm from the superior edge of the skin ellipse  8cm from the superior margin  6cm from the lateral margin  and 14cm from the inferior margin  This mass is located in the outer superior quadrant  1 2 o clock   There is another lesion measuring 3 x 2 x 2 5cm  which is white  firm  and irregular in shape  that extends 0 3cm from the closest  deep  margin  5cm from the superior margin  3 5cm from the medial margin  and 10cm from the inferior margin  This lesion is located in the inner superior quadrant  10 11 o clock  and is 1cm from the first described mass  This lesion has a safety pin  In the axillary tail  several lymph nodes are dissected ranging in size from from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to 1 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  SECTION CODE A  Additional superior margin  B  Additional axillary tissue  C  1 o clock lesion  closest margin  deep   D F  1 o clock lesion  G  11 o clock lesion  closest margin  deep   H  11 o clock lesion  closest margin  deep   I J  11 o clock lesion  K L  Breast parenchyma  M P  Lymph nodes  axillary tail  Resident  MONICA da SILVA NUNES  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Diane R Fingold  M D  Irene Kuter  M D  Dennis C Sgroi  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL SUPERFICIAL MARGIN    EXC PART C  LYMPH NODES  LEFT  ADDITIONAL AXILLARY TISSUE    E , Positive.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 11 43 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 3  REMOVED_DATE CM  INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS AND EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN ALONG A BROAD FRONT  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU CONFINED TO THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 38                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumor