    LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA  SENTINEL   EXCISION   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN 2 OF 5 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE ABOVE AND SUMMARY IN TABLE   2   NOTE  To evaluate for metastatic carcinoma  immunohistochemical stains for  cytokeratin  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2  cytokeratin 7  and pankeratin were examined on levels  from each of three blocks  The findings support the above diagnosis     LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY CONTENTS   DISSECTION   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 16 LYMPH NODES  SEE SUMMARY IN TABLE  2       TABLE OF PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS   2  SUMMARY OF AXILLARY LYMPH NODES    TOTAL NUMBER OF POSITIVE LYMPH NODES  2  sentinel nodes   TOTAL NUMBER OF LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  21  Number of lymph nodes with metastases 0 02cm or less  isolated tumor cells   0  Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 02cm to 0 2cm  micrometastases   0  Number of lymph nodes with metastases  0 2cm  macrometastases   2  Extracapsular extension  Marked   Other forms of axillary involvement  Lymphatic vessels       GROSS DESCRIPTION   Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  and  right axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm portion of yellow   lobulated  fibroadipose tissue  containing 5 tan pink candidate lymph nodes   measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm and 3 measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x  0 2cm  The largest lymph node is bisected and entirely frozen as  FX  1  now submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The middle sized lymph node is inked black   bisected and entirely frozen along with one of the small lymph nodes as FX 1A   now submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The remaining 2 lymph nodes are entirely submitted in  cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID      Received are 2 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN     Received fresh  labeled  right breast  short superior  long lateral   is a REMOVED_DATE  x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm mastectomy spec