Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 08 37 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 47                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 37 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a 2 8x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm fragment of breast  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 0 8cm firm  well circumscribed nodule abutting the inked margin  The nodule is submitted in casettes A and B  The remainders are submitted entirely in cassettes C and D  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS NODULE TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY    report_end  , Positive.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Updated Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery Unit Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  Resident  Matthew M Johnson  M D  Frozen Section Pathologist  Andrew E Rosenberg  MD Frozen Section Consultant s   Melinda J Lerwill  M D  Frozen Section Resident  James E  Davis  M D  Signed Out by  Joshua Kish  M D             Addended Report             Reason for Addendum  1  Additional Immunohistochemistry Results CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION  1  INVASIVE CARCINOMA  2 2 CM  WITH ADENOSQUAMOUS AND SPINDLE FEATURES  FOCALLY POSITIVE AT A TISSUE MARGIN  2  HEALING BIOPSY SITE   SEE NOTE   NOTE  This is an unusual carcinoma that consists of a relatively well circumscribed nodule of malignant cells with focal squamous differentiation and malignant spindle cells with a moderate mitotic rate  Focally  the spindle cells merge with the carcinoma cells supporting a histologic relationship  Immunohistochemical stains for heavy chain myosin  calponin  p63  and cytokeratin highlight the lack of myoepithelial cells around many of the glands as well as single epithelial cells  Stains for cytokeratin 903  wide spectrum keratin  and epithelial membrane antigen also highlight the single cells  The case has been reviewed with Drs  Sgroi  Koerner  and Lerwill who agree with the above interpretation  The results of immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and Her2 neu protein expression and of fluorescence in situ hybridization studies for Her2 neu gene amplification will be reported in an addendum  BREAST  LEFT  MEDIAL FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT  CEPHALAD FINAL SHAVED MARGIN   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST